Breaks: a purge claim on PostgreSQL and CockroachDB locks the object before the catalog's row, against the lock order every other write keeps (catalog first), so it can deadlock with a conditional grant on the object, which locks the catalog's row for update and then the object (backlog 171).
Module: catalog-store-sql
Test: SqlLockOrderTest#aPurgeClaimLocksTheCatalogTheObjectAndTheNamespacesAboveItBeforeReadingHolds

